    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d590">

                <pb facs="0729" n="609" xml:id="pg609"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Japanese
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November 8,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: The Department has
                    received to-day from our embassy at St. Petersburg a telegram which I quote for
                    your information: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The following telegram has been received from the Japanese minister at
                            Berlin, regarding question of clothing for prisoners: “As it is intended
                            to send a Japanese officer to arrange all matters with Russian
                            authorities before the departure of prisoners, he will also arrange
                            about clothing, if necessary.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
